    <ul>
      <li><strong>Pricing Based on Vanity Follower Counts:</strong> Quoting high rates based on 100k followers when your recent videos average 2k views leads to dissatisfied brands and negative campaign ROI. Always anchor pricing to consistent median views.</li>
      <li><strong>Giving Away Unlimited Usage Rights (In Perpetuity):</strong> Signing contracts granting brands perpetual commercial usage allows them to run ads featuring your face for years without paying another dollar. Always limit usage rights to 30, 60, or 90 days.</li>
      <li><strong>Failing to Account for Production Overhead:</strong> Forgetting to factor in camera gear, studio lighting, editing time, software subscriptions, props, and taxes leaves you with little net profit.</li>
      <li><strong>Working Without Upfront Deposits:</strong> Publishing sponsored content before receiving an upfront deposit (standard: 50% on signing) exposes you to payment delays and non-payment risk.</li>
      <li><strong>Promoting Products You Don't Believe In:</strong> Endorsing low-quality products for quick cash alienates your audience and destroys the organic trust that makes your channel valuable in the first place.</li>
    </ul>

    <h2>Best Practices for Landing and Managing Successful Brand Deals</h2>
    <p>
